What the recording should show
Make one short, continuous screen recording. Editing and camera video are not required. Your screen and voice should make it possible to follow:

the supplied code running on the original input;
the one input or parameter the task asks you to change;
the input and Python type used by each operation;
what each operation does and what it returns;
whether the model is reached through OpenRouter or Ollama;
what the output means for the week’s research question;
one important limit, connected to an essential reading.

Enter the OpenRouter key before recording, or use Ollama, so the key never appears on screen. Before uploading, play the first and last few seconds of the file and check that your voice is audible.

Complete this before Week 1
Follow the repository’s platform-specific setup guide. In outline:

install uv;
clone the complete repository or download and extract its ZIP;
open a terminal in that folder and run uv sync --frozen;
install Ollama;
run ollama pull gemma4:e2b-it-qat;
receive the OpenRouter key privately;
run uv run python scripts/preflight_models.py --live;
or complete the dual-route preflight notebook.

The preflight should show successful OpenRouter and Ollama calls without displaying the key. If the local model cannot run on your machine, complete those initial calls on a paired or instructor machine. Hardware ownership does not affect the mark.
Do not download a weekly .ipynb file by itself for local work. The notebooks also use the course configuration and, in some weeks, supplied images or data. The setup guide gives copyable Git and ZIP instructions for macOS, Windows and Linux.
